IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er4-nouns`
IMPORT `er4-part3-reg63-weekly-indemnity-plan`

-- Tests of reg 63 (SOR-96-332.txt lines 1039-1073). Every expected value is written by hand from the text.
-- Fixtures: a case that meets every paragraph, and one helper per paragraph that varies only that paragraph's
-- facts (there is no record-update operator, so each helper builds the whole record).

§ `Fixtures`

-- The events of 63(f)(i) to (iv).
`er4 test events 63(f)` MEANS LIST `er4 the end of a period during which the benefits are paid`
                                 , `er4 the end of the period of incapacity due to the illness or injury`
                                 , `er4 the date the insured person retires`
                                 , `er4 the date of the insured person's separation from employment for a reason other than illness or injury, notice having been given before the onset of the illness or the occurrence of the injury`

`er4 test no conditions` MEANS EMPTY

-- Ruler for the OF below:
--   hour-bank, commenced, eligible, day-400-hours, elim?, elim days, elim begins at first day, c(i), c(ii), weekly benefit, normal earnings, recurrence, new illness, weeks, events, conditions
GIVEN hb IS A BOOLEAN
      commenced IS A DATE
      eligible IS A DATE
      d400 IS A DATE
GIVETH A `er4 Case under a Weekly Indemnity Plan`
`er4 test case varying (a)` MEANS
    `er4 Case under a Weekly Indemnity Plan` OF hb, commenced, eligible, d400, TRUE, 7, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 550, 1000, 3, 1, 15, `er4 test events 63(f)`, `er4 test no conditions`

GIVEN req IS A BOOLEAN
      days IS A NUMBER
      begins IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `er4 Case under a Weekly Indemnity Plan`
`er4 test case varying (b)` MEANS
    `er4 Case under a Weekly Indemnity Plan` OF FALSE, YearMonthDay 2026 1 15, YearMonthDay 2026 5 1, YearMonthDay 2026 3 20, req, days, begins, TRUE, TRUE, 550, 1000, 3, 1, 15, `er4 test events 63(f)`, `er4 test no conditions`

GIVEN full1 IS A BOOLEAN
      full2 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `er4 Case under a Weekly Indemnity Plan`
`er4 test case varying (c)` MEANS
    `er4 Case under a Weekly Indemnity Plan` OF FALSE, YearMonthDay 2026 1 15, YearMonthDay 2026 5 1, YearMonthDay 2026 3 20, TRUE, 7, TRUE, full1, full2, 550, 1000, 3, 1, 15, `er4 test events 63(f)`, `er4 test no conditions`

GIVEN benefit IS A NUMBER
      earnings IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `er4 Case under a Weekly Indemnity Plan`
`er4 test case varying (d)` MEANS
    `er4 Case under a Weekly Indemnity Plan` OF FALSE, YearMonthDay 2026 1 15, YearMonthDay 2026 5 1, YearMonthDay 2026 3 20, TRUE, 7, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, benefit, earnings, 3, 1, 15, `er4 test events 63(f)`, `er4 test no conditions`

GIVEN hb IS A BOOLEAN
      recurrence IS A NUMBER
      newill IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `er4 Case under a Weekly Indemnity Plan`
`er4 test case varying (e)` MEANS
    `er4 Case under a Weekly Indemnity Plan` OF hb, YearMonthDay 2026 1 15, YearMonthDay 2026 5 1, YearMonthDay 2026 3 20, TRUE, 7, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 550, 1000, recurrence, newill, 15, `er4 test events 63(f)`, `er4 test no conditions`

GIVEN weeks IS A NUMBER
      events IS A LIST OF `er4 Event that ends payment of benefits under a plan`
GIVETH A `er4 Case under a Weekly Indemnity Plan`
`er4 test case varying (f)` MEANS
    `er4 Case under a Weekly Indemnity Plan` OF FALSE, YearMonthDay 2026 1 15, YearMonthDay 2026 5 1, YearMonthDay 2026 3 20, TRUE, 7, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 550, 1000, 3, 1, weeks, events, `er4 test no conditions`

GIVEN conditions IS A LIST OF `er4 Condition that precludes payment of benefits under a plan`
GIVETH A `er4 Case under a Weekly Indemnity Plan`
`er4 test case varying (g)` MEANS
    `er4 Case under a Weekly Indemnity Plan` OF FALSE, YearMonthDay 2026 1 15, YearMonthDay 2026 5 1, YearMonthDay 2026 3 20, TRUE, 7, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 550, 1000, 3, 1, 15, `er4 test events 63(f)`, conditions

§ `Reg 63(a) -- eligible on or before the first day of the month following the three months, or the 400 hours`

-- A period of three months beginning on 15 January 2026 ends on 14 April 2026; the first day of the next month is 1 May 2026.
#ASSERT `reg 63(a)(i) the last day of a period of three months of continuous employment beginning on` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 15) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 14
#ASSERT `reg 63(a)(i) the last day of a period of three months of continuous employment beginning on` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 3 31
#ASSERT `reg 63(a) the first day of the month following` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 14) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 5 1
#ASSERT `reg 63(a) the first day of the month following` (YearMonthDay 2026 12 31) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2027 1 1
-- Eligible on 1 May exactly ("on or before"): met. On 2 May: not met. Earlier: met.
#ASSERT `reg 63(a) the person becomes eligible to claim benefits under the plan in time` (`er4 test case varying (a)` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 20))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 63(a) the person becomes eligible to claim benefits under the plan in time` (`er4 test case varying (a)` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 5 2) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 20))
#ASSERT `reg 63(a) the person becomes eligible to claim benefits under the plan in time` (`er4 test case varying (a)` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 20))
-- An hour-bank plan: the day the person had 400 hours is 20 March 2026, so the bound is 1 April 2026 (the month limb no longer governs).
#ASSERT `reg 63(a) the person becomes eligible to claim benefits under the plan in time` (`er4 test case varying (a)` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 20))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 63(a) the person becomes eligible to claim benefits under the plan in time` (`er4 test case varying (a)` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 4 2) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 20))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 63(a) the person becomes eligible to claim benefits under the plan in time` (`er4 test case varying (a)` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 20))

§ `Reg 63(b) -- an elimination period of at most seven consecutive days from the first day of incapacity`

#ASSERT `reg 63(b) any elimination period does not exceed seven consecutive days beginning with the first day of the period of incapacity` (`er4 test case varying (b)` TRUE 7 TRUE)
#ASSERT `reg 63(b) any elimination period does not exceed seven consecutive days beginning with the first day of the period of incapacity` (`er4 test case varying (b)` TRUE 1 TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `reg 63(b) any elimination period does not exceed seven consecutive days beginning with the first day of the period of incapacity` (`er4 test case varying (b)` TRUE 8 TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `reg 63(b) any elimination period does not exceed seven consecutive days beginning with the first day of the period of incapacity` (`er4 test case varying (b)` TRUE 7 FALSE)
-- No elimination period at all: the paragraph asks nothing of the days.
#ASSERT `reg 63(b) any elimination period does not exceed seven consecutive days beginning with the first day of the period of incapacity` (`er4 test case varying (b)` FALSE 99 FALSE)

§ `Reg 63(c) -- benefits paid in full regardless of benefits under the Act and from other sources`

#ASSERT `reg 63(c) benefits are paid in full regardless of the benefits payable under the Act and from other sources` (`er4 test case varying (c)` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `reg 63(c) benefits are paid in full regardless of the benefits payable under the Act and from other sources` (`er4 test case varying (c)` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `reg 63(c) benefits are paid in full regardless of the benefits payable under the Act and from other sources` (`er4 test case varying (c)` TRUE FALSE)

§ `Reg 63(d) -- at least 55% of normal weekly insurable earnings`

-- 55% of 1000 is 550: "equal to or greater than" so 550 meets it and 549.99 does not.
#ASSERT `reg 63(d) the benefits payable under the plan are at least 55% of the normal weekly insurable earnings` (`er4 test case varying (d)` 550 1000)
#ASSERT `reg 63(d) the benefits payable under the plan are at least 55% of the normal weekly insurable earnings` (`er4 test case varying (d)` 551 1000)
#ASSERT NOT `reg 63(d) the benefits payable under the plan are at least 55% of the normal weekly insurable earnings` (`er4 test case varying (d)` 549.99 1000)

§ `Reg 63(e) -- reinstatement of full benefits`

-- Not hour-bank: three months on a recurrence, one month for a new illness.
#ASSERT `reg 63(e) full benefits are reinstated as the paragraph requires` (`er4 test case varying (e)` FALSE 3 1)
#ASSERT `reg 63(e) full benefits are reinstated as the paragraph requires` (`er4 test case varying (e)` FALSE 2 0)
#ASSERT NOT `reg 63(e) full benefits are reinstated as the paragraph requires` (`er4 test case varying (e)` FALSE 4 1)
#ASSERT NOT `reg 63(e) full benefits are reinstated as the paragraph requires` (`er4 test case varying (e)` FALSE 3 2)
#ASSERT `reg 63(e)(i) full benefits are reinstated in time on the recurrence of an illness or injury` (`er4 test case varying (e)` FALSE 3 2)
#ASSERT NOT `reg 63(e)(ii) full benefits are reinstated in time for a new illness or injury` (`er4 test case varying (e)` FALSE 3 2)
-- Hour-bank: the first 400 hours on a recurrence, the first 150 for a new illness.
#ASSERT `reg 63(e) full benefits are reinstated as the paragraph requires` (`er4 test case varying (e)` TRUE 400 150)
#ASSERT NOT `reg 63(e) full benefits are reinstated as the paragraph requires` (`er4 test case varying (e)` TRUE 401 150)
#ASSERT NOT `reg 63(e) full benefits are reinstated as the paragraph requires` (`er4 test case varying (e)` TRUE 400 151)

§ `Reg 63(f) -- benefits payable until the earliest of four events, for at least 15 weeks`

#ASSERT `reg 63(f) benefits are payable until the earliest of the four events` (`er4 test case varying (f)` 15 `er4 test events 63(f)`)
#ASSERT `reg 63(f) benefits are payable until the earliest of the four events` (`er4 test case varying (f)` 26 `er4 test events 63(f)`)
#ASSERT NOT `reg 63(f) benefits are payable until the earliest of the four events` (`er4 test case varying (f)` 14 `er4 test events 63(f)`)
-- The exhaustion of accumulated sick leave is not one of 63(f)'s four events, nor is any other event.
#ASSERT NOT `reg 63(f) benefits are payable until the earliest of the four events` (`er4 test case varying (f)` 15 (LIST `er4 the end of a period during which the benefits are paid`, `er4 the exhaustion of all accumulated paid sick leave`))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 63(f) benefits are payable until the earliest of the four events` (`er4 test case varying (f)` 15 (LIST `er4 any other event`))
#ASSERT `reg 63(f) an event at which payment under the plan may end` `er4 the date the insured person retires`
#ASSERT NOT `reg 63(f) an event at which payment under the plan may end` `er4 the exhaustion of all accumulated paid sick leave`

§ `Reg 63(g) -- only the seventeen listed conditions may preclude payment`

-- A plan that precludes payment only for the first, third and fifteenth conditions.
#ASSERT `reg 63(g) the only conditions precluding payment are conditions the paragraph lists` (`er4 test case varying (g)` (LIST `er4 the person is not under the care of a licensed physician`, `er4 the illness or injury is intentionally self-inflicted`, `er4 the person is receiving a retirement pension from the employer`))
-- No precluding condition at all: nothing outside the list.
#ASSERT `reg 63(g) the only conditions precluding payment are conditions the paragraph lists` (`er4 test case varying (g)` EMPTY)
-- A condition on no line of the list defeats the paragraph.
#ASSERT NOT `reg 63(g) the only conditions precluding payment are conditions the paragraph lists` (`er4 test case varying (g)` (LIST `er4 the person is not under the care of a licensed physician`, `er4 a condition not listed in paragraph 63(g)`))
-- (ii) only where the amounts paid under those laws are earnings under s 35.
#ASSERT `reg 63(g) a condition that may preclude payment of benefits under the plan` (`er4 the illness or injury is covered by workers' compensation law, the Canada Pension Plan or the Quebec Pension Plan` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `reg 63(g) a condition that may preclude payment of benefits under the plan` (`er4 the illness or injury is covered by workers' compensation law, the Canada Pension Plan or the Quebec Pension Plan` FALSE)
-- (x) only if the right is reinstated on return to active employment.
#ASSERT `reg 63(g) a condition that may preclude payment of benefits under the plan` (`er4 the person becomes ill or is injured after having lost employment by reason of a stoppage of work attributable to a labour dispute at the place where the person was employed` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `reg 63(g) a condition that may preclude payment of benefits under the plan` (`er4 the person becomes ill or is injured after having lost employment by reason of a stoppage of work attributable to a labour dispute at the place where the person was employed` FALSE)
-- (xiii) only for a person not receiving continuing treatment.
#ASSERT `reg 63(g) a condition that may preclude payment of benefits under the plan` (`er4 the illness results from the use of drugs or alcohol` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `reg 63(g) a condition that may preclude payment of benefits under the plan` (`er4 the illness results from the use of drugs or alcohol` FALSE)
-- (xvi) except where the surgery is needed because of an illness or injury.
#ASSERT `reg 63(g) a condition that may preclude payment of benefits under the plan` (`er4 the person is absent from work because of plastic surgery performed solely for cosmetic purposes` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `reg 63(g) a condition that may preclude payment of benefits under the plan` (`er4 the person is absent from work because of plastic surgery performed solely for cosmetic purposes` FALSE)
-- (xvii) where the reinstatement period does not exceed six months.
#ASSERT `reg 63(g) a condition that may preclude payment of benefits under the plan` (`er4 the person with a recurring disability is receiving benefits under a group long-term disability plan that contains a reinstatement provision` 6)
#ASSERT NOT `reg 63(g) a condition that may preclude payment of benefits under the plan` (`er4 the person with a recurring disability is receiving benefits under a group long-term disability plan that contains a reinstatement provision` 7)
-- A plain listed condition, with no limit of its own.
#ASSERT `reg 63(g) a condition that may preclude payment of benefits under the plan` `er4 the person is an inmate of a prison or similar institution`

§ `Reg 63 -- all seven together`

#ASSERT `reg 63 the plan meets the requirements of a Weekly Indemnity Plan` (`er4 test case varying (a)` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 20))
-- Failing any one paragraph fails the whole.
#ASSERT NOT `reg 63 the plan meets the requirements of a Weekly Indemnity Plan` (`er4 test case varying (a)` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 5 2) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 20))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 63 the plan meets the requirements of a Weekly Indemnity Plan` (`er4 test case varying (b)` TRUE 8 TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `reg 63 the plan meets the requirements of a Weekly Indemnity Plan` (`er4 test case varying (c)` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `reg 63 the plan meets the requirements of a Weekly Indemnity Plan` (`er4 test case varying (d)` 549 1000)
#ASSERT NOT `reg 63 the plan meets the requirements of a Weekly Indemnity Plan` (`er4 test case varying (e)` FALSE 4 1)
#ASSERT NOT `reg 63 the plan meets the requirements of a Weekly Indemnity Plan` (`er4 test case varying (f)` 14 `er4 test events 63(f)`)
#ASSERT NOT `reg 63 the plan meets the requirements of a Weekly Indemnity Plan` (`er4 test case varying (g)` (LIST `er4 a condition not listed in paragraph 63(g)`))
